---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Justin McBroom — JustinCredibleTech is the long-form companion to @JCredibleTech: consumer tech, space, science, Tesla/SpaceX/xAI/Starlink/EV."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="page-header" style="max-width: none; margin-bottom: 0;">
      <h1>About JustinCredibleTech</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="font-family: var(--font-sans); margin-top: 0;">
        Long-form companion to <strong>@JCredibleTech</strong> — for when a post needs room to breathe.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p>
      Hey — I’m <strong>Justin McBroom</strong>. Online you’ll usually see me as
      <a href="https://x.com/JCredibleTech" rel="noopener noreferrer">@JCredibleTech</a>.
      Short posts are great for the “wait, what just shipped?” moments. This site is for the
      follow-up: context, timelines, and the “why should I care?” without the fluff.
    </p>

    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
    <p>
      JustinCredibleTech covers the beat I already chase in socials — consumer tech drops,
      spaceflight milestones, and science that actually touches technology. Think new phones and
      foldables, lunar AI models, Starlink coverage leaps, EV and robotaxi reality checks, and the
      companies that keep showing up in that orbit: <strong>Tesla, SpaceX, xAI, Starlink</strong>,
      and the broader EV / space / AI stack.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consumer tech</strong> — launches, specs that matter, and what “available Friday” really means.</li>
      <li><strong>Space</strong> — missions, maps, and orbital internet that changes who gets a signal.</li>
      <li><strong>Science × tech</strong> — open models, ice prospectivity, sensors, and tools researchers can actually download.</li>
      <li><strong>Mobility &amp; energy</strong> — EVs, autonomy, and the infrastructure that makes the demos stick.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How I write</h2>
    <p>
      Voice check: lighthearted, informative, and fun. I aim for accurate facts, clear structure,
      and zero politics. If a rumor isn’t confirmed, I’ll say so. If Apple, NASA, or SpaceX
      published a date and a price, you’ll get those — not vibes dressed up as news.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reading experience matters too. Articles here are set for long-form: comfortable line length,
      readable type, and the basics done right — RSS, sitemap, and sensible SEO titles so you can
      subscribe or share without fighting the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Free to host, yours to fork</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a static Astro build on purpose. Drop the <code>dist/</code> folder on Netlify,
      point Cloudflare Pages at the repo, or self-host the HTML. Custom domains can wait until
      you’re ready to pay for one. The content should travel light.
    </p>

    <p>
      Glad you’re here. Start with the <a href={withBase("blog/")}>latest posts</a>, or grab the
      <a href={withBase("rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a> and read on your own schedule.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
